# Check out LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true gives Windows working trees CRLF while Biome's
# formatter enforces LF — so `pnpm lint` fails on ~24 untouched files immediately
# after any clone or branch switch, and `biome format --write .` has to be re-run
# every time. CI runs on Linux and never sees it. See bd mastra-chat-kit-b5g.
#
# Git already stores LF (autocrlf normalised on commit), so this changes what lands
# in the working tree, not repository content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.db  binary
